# elohim-hub — peer application serving

The [root lifecycle map](../../.epr-meta/manifest.md#application-lifecycle--authoritative-homes-and-composition)
routes applications here for peer-native serving. The existing
[hub boundary design](../../genesis/docs/content/elohim-protocol/architecture/2026-05-02-elohim-hub-boundaries-design.md)
owns the split; [this directory's placement guide](README.md#the-web-seam) describes
the test and current implementation debt. Follow that guide when extending the
runtime code and its manifest-owned gate.

Own app-file serving, rendering and deliverability when a peer can be addressed and
verified by key. Compose storage's verified bytes and head decisions; do not elect a
new canonical head based on what can render. A locally held usable version can be
served with its observed status. SDK/storage own working-state persistence and sync;
doorway owns browser/web2 accommodation. The same peer service must work without a
doorway, and the hub must not depend on doorway names or certificates. Test peer-local
serving before claiming its doorway projection delivers the same capability. Review
and existing storage/doorway placement advisories hold this boundary today.
